# OLIVE BRANCH — Docker build-context exclusions.
#
# .gitignore keeps tools/jitsi-selfhost/.jitsi-docker/ out of git, but
# .gitignore has no effect on `docker build`'s own context — a real,
# already-generated .jitsi-docker/.env (holding live Prosody/Jicofo/JVB/
# Jigasi/Jibri auth secrets) sat inside this Dockerfile's `COPY . .` scope
# with nothing to stop it landing permanently in the image's layer
# history, confirmed as a live leak path on a machine where the Jitsi
# self-host setup had already run. This file closes that.

# Vendored third-party checkout + generated secrets — same reasoning as
# the root .gitignore's identical entry, restated here because .gitignore
# does not reach Docker's own build context. It's also a nested git
# checkout with its own .git/ history, which would otherwise sweep in
# here too.
tools/jitsi-selfhost/.jitsi-docker/

# Reinstalled fresh by `npm ci` inside the image (the Dockerfile's own
# COPY order already relies on this for layer-cache reasons) — the host's
# own copy is frequently built for a different OS/arch and should never
# be copied in regardless.
node_modules/

# This repo's own git history has no reason to enter a runtime image.
.git/
.gitignore

# Local dev secrets for docker-compose.dev.yml itself (SESSION_SECRET,
# DEV_LOGIN) — read from the environment at container start, never baked
# into an image layer. See .env.example, which stays trackable.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS/editor cruft.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
